WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.150
Flick the switch on a fan,
and it spins straight away.

2
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.930
No engine. No fuel.

3
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:08.990
Just a current in some wire,
and a couple of magnets.

4
00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:11.870
So what is actually pushing it round?

5
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:15.140
Let's build the answer,
one step at a time.

6
00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:17.320
Start with a picture.

7
00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:21.000
Imagine water in a stream,
swirling round a post.

8
00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:25.950
Keep that stream in mind, because a
magnetic field behaves a lot like it.

9
00:00:26.767 --> 00:00:29.227
Here is a straight wire,
with compasses around it.

10
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.977
Switch on a current, and the needles
swing round to point in circles.

11
00:00:34.027 --> 00:00:36.627
A current makes a magnetic
field around the wire,

12
00:00:36.667 --> 00:00:38.697
like the swirl round the post.

13
00:00:38.747 --> 00:00:43.497
The swirl is strongest close to the wire,
and a bigger current makes it stronger.

14
00:00:43.547 --> 00:00:46.877
Reverse the current, and the
swirl turns the other way.

15
00:00:46.927 --> 00:00:49.487
Pause here, and try it yourself.

16
00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:52.980
Now wind the wire into a coil.

17
00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:55.090
This is called a solenoid.

18
00:00:55.740 --> 00:01:00.570
The swirls from every turn join up inside,
like small streams joining into one

19
00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:02.600
strong, steady flow.

20
00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:06.220
Outside, the field has the
same shape as a bar magnet's.

21
00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:10.500
Slide in an iron core, and
the field gets stronger still.

22
00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:15.080
That is an electromagnet: a
magnet you can switch on and off.

23
00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:17.330
Pause, and try it.

24
00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:21.760
That is everything Foundation tier needs.

25
00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:26.070
The rest is Higher tier:
how this makes a motor turn.

26
00:01:26.793 --> 00:01:30.023
Put a wire carrying a
current between two magnets.

27
00:01:30.073 --> 00:01:34.583
The magnets' field is a steady
stream, flowing from north to south.

28
00:01:34.633 --> 00:01:36.943
The current adds its own swirl.

29
00:01:36.993 --> 00:01:40.463
On one side of the wire, the
swirl runs with the stream.

30
00:01:40.513 --> 00:01:42.963
On the other side, it runs against it.

31
00:01:43.013 --> 00:01:47.303
So the wire is pushed sideways, and
the magnets are pushed the other way.

32
00:01:47.353 --> 00:01:50.393
This push is called the motor effect.

33
00:01:51.327 --> 00:01:52.837
Which way is the push?

34
00:01:52.887 --> 00:01:55.057
Use Fleming's left-hand rule.

35
00:01:55.107 --> 00:01:56.797
First finger for the field.

36
00:01:56.847 --> 00:01:58.777
Second finger for the current.

37
00:01:58.827 --> 00:02:00.817
Your thumb shows the force.

38
00:02:00.867 --> 00:02:05.927
Pause, and predict: what happens to
the force if the current is reversed?

39
00:02:07.633 --> 00:02:09.743
Now look at the whole coil.

40
00:02:09.793 --> 00:02:14.463
The current flows one way along this side,
and back the other way along that side.

41
00:02:14.513 --> 00:02:18.403
So one side is pushed up,
and the other is pushed down.

42
00:02:18.453 --> 00:02:21.863
Like a paddle wheel in the
stream, the coil turns.

43
00:02:21.913 --> 00:02:25.713
Pause, and predict what
flipping the magnets would do.

44
00:02:27.117 --> 00:02:29.467
Watch out for one common mistake.

45
00:02:29.517 --> 00:02:32.107
The magnets do not pull the coil round.

46
00:02:32.157 --> 00:02:34.567
Copper is not attracted to magnets.

47
00:02:34.617 --> 00:02:37.527
Switch the current off,
and the forces vanish.

48
00:02:37.577 --> 00:02:39.937
No current, no force.

49
00:02:40.797 --> 00:02:41.797
Quick check.

50
00:02:41.837 --> 00:02:45.427
Why do the two sides of the coil
move in opposite directions?

51
00:02:45.477 --> 00:02:48.667
Because the current flows in
opposite directions in them.

52
00:02:48.717 --> 00:02:52.797
So, in one line: a current in
a magnetic field feels a force,

53
00:02:52.837 --> 00:02:55.147
and that force turns the motor.
